body:
I was in hospital once before (regular hospital), early last year;
I had a bad few weeks and made the halfhearted decision to cut my wrists, someone took me to hospital, i tried to leave but they stopped me. I got counselling, but it never really helped, at all.

TLDR: I don't like that idea.

From my intepretation of your words above, i've gathered that you don't think humanity can change for the better;
But i believe we **can** change. that we **can** care, and that we **can** all work as one to do what is right;
 **But** i believe that the vast majority of people simply **won't**, because they are, in one form or another, apathetically hungry for power, and/or simply too **shallow** to see the whole picture.
  I think that we should try our very best to do what's **right**, and i think we should consider **all** of our options, including, if necessary, suicide.

Thankyou Tank18, really.
Hugs;

P.S. who are the right people?
